uties.”  Mogadishu is a city that is not in this polity but is in some ways comparable as a Muslim trading city: "Ibn Battuta\'s description of Mogadishu indicates that the city was highly advanced as a center of trade and Islamic learning." "The three Muslim States of Ifat, Hadya and Fatajar occupied the strategic positions that provided footholds for further penetration of Islamic commerce and learning into the Christian kingdom of Ethiopia."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2330, 'temperature': 0.2})
